					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-08-06 | Monday</font></strong><br><br><div align="center"><strong>JFK to LAX.</strong><br /></div><br />flew into the City of Angels this morning and drove out to San Diego to get ready for our events with <strong><a href="http://www.pnoyapparel.com/">PnoyApp</a></strong>.  we&#39;ll be updating the bloggy blog soon with more photos of the NYC segment of the trip soon, for now tho, gotta nap.

<br /><br />-sabba ranks<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-08-05 | Sunday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://green-street.net/green-street/Images/dna_lounge/blue_scholars/11699-geologic.jpg" alt="" width="320" height="480" /><br /><br /><img src="http://green-street.net/green-street/Images/dna_lounge/blue_scholars/11707-blue_scholars.jpg" alt="" width="320" height="480" /><br /><br />Hello world! Being the nice guy that I am, I&#39;m here to share with y&#39;all a live set by Blue Scholars that maybe the BS themselves might not even own! On July 7, 2005, the Scholars opened up for Chali 2na and Crown City Rockers at the DNA Lounge, located in the Bay Area. <br /><br />Stay tuned, cuz I might post up another BS live performance if y&#39;all are nice enough. Remember to sign in to the ever-growing forums and let us know what y&#39;all think about the blog, the site, the artists, and more.<br /><br />Blue Scholars - Live, DNA Lounge, SF:<br />http://www.zshare.net/audio/3004955f0c1e39/<br /><br /><em>Above photos from the DNA Lounge show courtesy of green-street.net!<br /></em><br />Peace<br />daps<em><br /></em> <p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-08-04 | Saturday</font></strong><br><br>As you might have heard, <strong>Sabzi</strong> and I are perusing <strong>NYC</strong> for the weekend. Taking a dinner break before heading out the <a href="http://www.apiasummit.com"><strong>APIA Spoken Word &amp; Poetry Summit</strong></a>
showcase tonight. It&#39;s been 6 years since the first one in Seattle, and
it&#39;s good to see folks still doing their thing, pushing the medium
forward while keeping this necessary space intact and open. Big up to<br />the
NYC organizing committee and see yall tomorrow (Sunday, August 5) in
Queens (Terazza Cafe, Jackson Heights, All-Ages). Blue Scholars willbe
rocking a <strong>Bayan-USA</strong> fundraiser with <strong>Kiwi</strong> (first show back from the Philippines), <strong>Koba</strong> and a bunch of folkers (<a href="http://www.myspace.com/bluescholars">more info here</a>).<br /><br /><br /><br />Taken from the homie <strong>Dandiggity</strong>&#39;s blog:<br /><br /><br /><br /><blockquote><em>The
APIA Spoken Word &amp; Poetry Summit is a biennial gathering of
progressive artists involved in the Asian Pacific Islander American
community. Our mission is to challenge the often peripheral and passive
roles the artist is branded within the APIA community and the arts
community at-large and to acknowledge the arts as a critical, elemental
component in building, empowering and transforming our community and
our selves. Please join us for a night of poetry and spoken word by the
nation&#39;s leading APIA performers and writers! Don&#39;t wait another two
years to see what this community is about! Hosted by Dandiggity, beats
by DJ Boo.<br /><br />  <br /><br />Sat, August 4th 8pm <br />4th National Asian Pacific Islander-American<br />Spoken Word and Poetry Summit Showcase<br />@ Judson Memorial Church // 273 Thompson St<br />between Sullivan St. and LaGuardia Pl.<br />$8-25 Sliding Scale<br /><br />  </em></blockquote>Peace<br />
Geo<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-08-03 | Friday</font></strong><br><br>Yo what&#39;s up peoples? I go by the name of DJ Nphared, I try to be around Seattle as much as I can, you can catch me doing my thing on stage with Grynch and my Sportn&#39; Life family. I was graciously brought on by the Mass Line brethren to offer a different prespective into this thing called hip-hop. I&#39;m gonna put yall on to artists you might not know about, and if you do, keep you up-to-date with the latest from them. I try not to sugar coat things and you will definitely learn that honesty is my best policy. I won&#39;t be a Simon Cowell about it, but I do wear my heart on my sleeve, so expect some of my emotion and soul to bleed into these posts. Shouts to all of the Mass Line fam-a-lam, STAY TUNED YALL!<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-08-03 | Friday</font></strong><br><br>What&#39;s good, fam? I&#39;m writing this in the midst of a mad dash to cram everything I own into back of a Subaru, so if it&#39;s brief, my apologies. I&#39;m leaving the city I love for Chicago in about 6 hours. Crazy. The realization that I own more studio equipment than clothing was trumped only by the realization that a station wagon ain&#39;t as big as it looks. This is not fun. Packing play-by-play and sentimentalism aside, I&#39;ve got a bit of tech-shit to speak on...<br /><br />Google Phone? You best believe it. The search and internet marketing masters have been scrambling to acquire a chunk of the wireless radio spectrum (the 700 mhz band to be precise) in the hopes of being able to provide some open source cell phone access for the masses. Open source=consumer freedom. Hotness. Whether or not Google manages to win the rights to use the 700 mhz band, the company <em>is</em> getting close to dropping some Google-branded handsets on the unsuspecting masses. The joint above is an artist rendering, but expect the final product include mobile versions of every imaginable Google App, from GChat, to Google Maps, to integrated search. If it looks anything like the joint above, I&#39;m sold. Byebye iPhone. <br /><br />On that note, fam, I&#39;m out. I will miss y&#39;all dearly, but the Chi is calling.<br /><br />Budo<br /> <p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> [23] <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from